1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,340
USA or China.

2
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:02,890
Who's winning the AI race?

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,290
Let's check the scoreboard.

4
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:06,340
Round one: the smartest AI.

5
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:10,250
The best American model beats the best Chinese one by just two point seven percent.

6
00:00:10,270 --> 00:00:12,770
Three years ago, that gap was huge.

7
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:14,690
Point, USA. Barely.

8
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:16,540
Round two: computing power.

9
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:20,060
America has about seventy-two percent of the world's AI computing power.

10
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,510
China? About ten.

11
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:23,190
Point, USA. Easily.

12
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:25,050
Round three: electricity.

13
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:29,650
AI eats power, and China is adding power plants about six times faster than America.

14
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:30,850
Point, China.

15
00:00:30,970 --> 00:00:32,360
Round four: the shock.

16
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:39,530
In January twenty twenty-five, a cheap Chinese AI called DeepSeek wiped nearly six hundred billion dollars off Nvidia in one day.

17
00:00:39,550 --> 00:00:41,870
Point, China. Two, two.

18
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,090
So, who wins?

19
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:46,440
Right now, America leads.

20
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,700
But China is catching up, fast and cheap.

21
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:49,740
The race isn't over.

22
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,390
It's barely past the first lap.

23
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:52,490
Follow for more.
